<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">deadeye</ansi>

The Deadeye is the neutral elite of the Sharpshooter (Arbalist route; no
alignment asked). A critical bolt needs no winding, and at the top rank
neither does a bolt that fells its foe; the Piercing Bolt also comes a round
sooner.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Hair trigger       a critical bolt needs no winding
  35 Killer's sight     +22% critical chance with a shooting weapon in all
  40 Steadier hands     Steady Aim gives +30 Attack
  45 Dead calm          +8 Attack with a shooting weapon in all
  50 Quickened loading  Piercing Bolt's cooldown is a round shorter
  55 Eagle's eye        +30% critical chance with a shooting weapon in all
  60 Ready again        a bolt that fells its foe needs no winding

It needs the Sharpshooter first (<ansi fg="command">help arbalist-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] deadeye confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Arbalist talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Long Draw (+10% damage with a
shooting weapon), Eagle Eye (+5 Attack with a shooting weapon), Quick Nock
(starts a battle with 15 points on its action meter). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help arbalist-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help arbalist</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
